Message(id='msg_01Cfx7esNCe7PQkKirN3Lpne', container=None, content=[TextBlock(citations=None, text='Here\'s a summary of all 5 files read in parallel:\n\n---\n\n## 📁 `agents/s01_agent_loop.py` — The Agent Loop\nThe **foundational pattern** of an AI coding agent. It implements the minimal core loop:\n- Uses a **single `bash` tool** to interact with the real world.\n- Loops with `while True`, calling the LLM, executing `tool_use` blocks, and feeding results back until `stop_reason != "tool_use"`.\n- Includes a simple dangerous-command blocklist and a 120s timeout.\n\n---\n\n## 📁 `agents/s02_tool_use.py` — Tool Dispatch\nBuilds on `s01` by **expanding the toolset** without changing the loop structure.\n- Adds `read_file`, `write_file`, and `edit_file` tools alongside `bash`.\n- Introduces a **`TOOL_HANDLERS` dispatch map** (`{tool_name: handler}`) to cleanly route tool calls.\n- Adds a `safe_path()` guard to prevent path traversal outside the workspace.\n\n---\n\n## 📁 `agents/s03_todo_write.py` — TodoWrite (Planning)\nIntroduces **self-tracked planning** via a `TodoManager` class.\n- A `todo` tool lets the model write/update a structured task list with `pending`, `in_progress`, and `completed` states.\n- Enforces only one `in_progress` item at a time (max 20 todos).\n- A **nag reminder** is injected into tool results if the model hasn\'t updated todos in 3+ rounds, with escalating urgency.\n- Enables extended thinking (`budget_tokens: 10000`).\n\n---\n\n## 📁 `agents/s04_subagent.py` — Subagents (Context Isolation)\nIntroduces **context isolation** through child agent spawning.\n- A `task` tool in the parent agent spawns a `run_subagent()` with a **fresh `messages=[]`** context.\n- The subagent shares the filesystem but **not** conversation history.\n- The child gets all base tools *except* `task` (no recursive spawning).\n- Only the final summary text is returned to the parent — the child\'s full context is discarded, keeping the parent clean.\n\n---\n\n## 📁 `agents/s05_skill_loading.py` — Skill Loading (On-Demand Knowledge)\nImplements **two-layer lazy knowledge injection** via a `SkillLoader` class.\n- **Layer 1** (cheap): Skill *names + descriptions* are listed in the system prompt (~100 tokens/skill).\n- **Layer 2** (on-demand): When the model calls `load_skill("name")`, the **full `SKILL.md` body** is returned in the `tool_result`.\n- Skills live under `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter (`name`, `description`, `tags`) and a markdown body.\n- Key insight: *"Don\'t put everything in the system prompt. Load on demand."*\n\n---\n\n### 🔁 Evolution Summary\n| File | Key Addition |\n|---|---|\n| `s01` | Core `while tool_use` loop + `bash` |\n| `s02` | Multi-tool dispatch map + path safety |\n| `s03` | Self-tracked planning + nag reminder |\n| `s04` | Subagent spawning + context isolation |\n| `s05` | Two-layer lazy skill loading |', type='text')], model='claude-sonnet-4-6', role='assistant', stop_details=None, stop_reason='end_turn', stop_sequence=None, type='message', usage=Usage(cache_creation=CacheCreation(ephemeral_1h_input_tokens=0, ephemeral_5m_input_tokens=0), cache_creation_input_tokens=0, cache_read_input_tokens=0, inference_geo='global', input_tokens=12224, output_tokens=833, server_tool_use=None, service_tier='standard'))
